Maroon 5 performed "This Love" live on ''[[Saturday Night Live]]'' (''SNL'') in February 2004.<ref>{{cite episode |title=Christina Aguilera/Maroon 5|series=Saturday Night Live |network=[[NBC]]|airdate=2004-02-21 |season=[[Saturday Night Live (season 29)|29]] |number=558 |minutes=90-92 }}</ref> The band won the [[MTV Video Music Award for Best New Artist]] for the music video of "This Love" in 2004.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.people.com/people/article/0,,689487,00.html|title=Jay-Z, OutKast Tie for 4 MTV Video Awards|last=Silverman|first=Stephen M.|date=August 30, 2004|work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|access-date=May 5, 2009|archive-date=June 2, 2009|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090602115125/http://www.people.com/people/article/0,,689487,00.html|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.foxnews.com/story/outkast-jay-z-big-winners-at-patriotic-vmas|title=OutKast, Jay-Z Big Winners at Patriotic VMAs|date=August 30, 2004|publisher=[[Fox News Channel|Fox News]]|access-date=May 4, 2009|archive-date=October 22, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121022102555/http://www.foxnews.com/story/0,2933,130493,00.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Also the same year, the song won for Choice Rock Track at the [[Teen Choice Award]]s.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://findarticles.com/p/articles/mi_m0EIN/is_2004_June_8/ai_n6058341/|title=Maroon 5 to Release Live/Acoustic EP; Nabs Five Teen Choice Nominations; Announces Summer Slate of Television Appearances|date=June 8, 2004|publisher=[[Business Wire]]|access-date=May 4, 2009|archive-date=January 21, 2007|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070121222353/http://findarticles.com/p/articles/mi_m0EIN/is_2004_June_8/ai_n6058341|url-status=usurped}}</ref> In the [[Nielsen Broadcast Data Systems]], "This Love" was the third played song of 2004, having 438,589 total plays.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.vh1.com/artists/news/1495342/20050105/maroon_5.jhtml|title=Usher's 'Yeah!' Was Most Played Song Of 2004|last=Vineyard|first=Jennifer|date=January 5, 2005|work=[[MTV News]]|publisher=[[VH1]]|access-date=May 4, 2009|archive-date=June 5, 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110605014158/http://www.vh1.com/artists/news/1495342/20050105/maroon_5.jhtml|url-status=dead}}</ref> At the [[48th Grammy Awards]], the song won a [[Grammy Award]] in the category for [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocals|Best Pop Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocal]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.cnn.com/2006/SHOWBIZ/Music/02/09/grammys.list/index.html |title=List of Grammy winners |date=February 9, 2006 |publisher=[[CNN|CNN: Showbiz/Music]] |access-date=May 4, 2009 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091125172301/http://www.cnn.com/2006/SHOWBIZ/Music/02/09/grammys.list/index.html |archive-date=November 25, 2009 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.foxnews.com/story/complete-list-of-48th-annual-grammy-award-winners|title=Complete List of 48th Annual Grammy Award Winners|date=February 8, 2006|agency=[[Associated Press]]|publisher=[[Fox News Channel|Fox News]]|access-date=May 4, 2009|archive-date=March 6, 2009|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090306172656/http://www.foxnews.com/story/0,2933,184295,00.html|url-status=live}}</ref>
{{Clear}}

sections.text:
thumb|left|Adam Levine singing "This Love" at the 2009 [[First inauguration of Barack Obama#Inaugural balls|Neighborhood Inauguration Ball]]

Maroon 5 performed "This Love" live on Saturday Night Live (SNL) in February 2004. The band won the MTV Video Music Award for Best New Artist for the music video of "This Love" in 2004. Also the same year, the song won for Choice Rock Track at the Teen Choice Awards. In the Nielsen Broadcast Data Systems, "This Love" was the third played song of 2004, having 438,589 total plays. At the 48th Grammy Awards, the song won a Grammy Award in the category for Best Pop Performance by a Duo or Group with Vocal.
{{Clear}}

